ginal recipe in Henry Hartshorne's the Household Cyclopedia.<ref>{{cite book |last=Hartshorne |first=Henry |author-link= |date=1881 |title=The Household Cyclopedia |url=https://archive.org/details/Household_Cyclopedia/mode/2up |location= |publisher= |page=321 |isbn=}}</ref> \n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 slice of [[Cookbook:Ham|ham]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] fine\n* 1 breast of roasted [[Cookbook:Poultry|fowl]], chopped fine\n* 1 pickled [[Cookbook:Cucumber|cucumber]], chopped fine \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Hard Boiled Eggs|hard-boiled egg]] yolk, [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Anchovy|anchovy]], minced\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]], minced \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallot]], chopped fine \n* 200 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] catsup ([[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]])\n\n==Procedure==\n# Combine all the ingredients together.\n# [[Cookbook:Boil|Boil]] this mixture until warm and serve.\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes using anchovy]]\n[[Category:Household Cyclopedia sauce recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg yolk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber pickles]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ham]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parsley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shallot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Nonpareil Sauce (Hartshorne)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 slice of ham, chopped fine","sourceText":"1 slice of ham, chopped fine","amountText":"1 slice of ham, chopped fine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 breast of roasted fowl, chopped fine","sourceText":"1 breast of roasted fowl, chopped fine","amountText":"1 breast of roasted fowl, chopped fine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 pickled cucumber, chopped fine","sourceText":"1 pickled cucumber, c